P18-V01 `countInnerMsgNum` cursor disposition — 2026-10-22 20:32 UTC

Reviewed pinned Java `MessageDecoder.countInnerMsgNum` and its call graph.
Java advances the input buffer through the compact batch. The only production
caller, `SendMessageProcessor`, wraps the message body in a temporary
`ByteBuffer`, uses the returned count for `PROPERTY_INNER_NUM`, and discards
the buffer. Rust's immutable-slice `count_inner_messages` preserves the count
and omits this unobserved cursor state; the existing compact fixture covers
valid counts and malformed-size outcomes. The API map and audit record this
source-confirmed API-shape adaptation. Docs-only update; no tests were run.
